&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the test strategy that protects Graphcore’s system software releases at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff System Software Engineer, you will shape integration and system testing across firmware, BMC and Linux device drivers. Your work will help create a high quality gate for system software release packages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, build, automate and report tests across complex server class systems. You will also develop reusable tools, pipelines and packaging solutions that help teams move faster with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role needs deep low level software knowledge and strong system thinking. You will own hard technical areas, guide best practice and stay close to the code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a new integration and system test team within System Software QA. The team verifies integrated components across BMC, firmware and Linux device drivers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work happens close to the hardware, across component teams and QA. You will partner with developers, consult package stakeholders and turn use cases into robust system tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decisions are shaped by evidence, clear technical reasoning and ownership. You will be expected to speak up, act fast and raise standards through hands-on leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Strong experience in low level system testing and integration across complex software and hardware layers.&lt;br&gt;· Deep understanding of RTOS, complex boot logic, Linux and device drivers.&lt;br&gt;· Test development capability using Python and C/C++.&lt;br&gt;· Experience working with hardware, debuggers, CI/CD pipelines and build or integration tools.&lt;br&gt;· Ability to debug cross-layer issues and drive root-cause investigations to lasting corrective actions.&lt;br&gt;· Clear communication skills, with the ability to mentor engineers and document complex technical decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. If you meet most of our essential criteria, we encourage you to submit an application and showcase how your background makes you a strong candidate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
